--!strict
--[[ T15 workstream 7a: what does a `require` of Facet COST IN MEMORY?

	ONE SUBSET PER PROCESS, on purpose: `require` is process-cached, so measuring
	two subsets in one VM measures the second one against the first one's leavings.
	The driver (`_probe_t15_mem_all`) re-launches this script once per subset.

	`gcinfo()` is the live-set probe (Lune has no forced collection). A REQUIRE is
	the one thing it reads honestly: a required module is RETAINED, so the delta is
	live memory rather than garbage in flight. The floor is sampled after the test
	harness itself is loaded and before the subject, so the number is the subject's.

	Usage: lune run tools/lune/_probe_t15_mem <subset>
]]
